    "cards": [
      [
        "Conflict can consist of waiting",
        "A collective first-person voice presents soldiers exposed to cold, exhaustion and uncertainty. The distant sounds of fighting do not make the immediate conditions harmless. The poem can shift a reader’s attention from spectacular action to sustained bodily and psychological pressure. The speakers’ suffering is an event even where expected action does not arrive."
      ],
      [
        "Nature and memory unsettle security",
        "Weather is presented through hostile imagery, while imagined or remembered home offers a different warmth. Yet the movement towards home does not provide a secure escape: closed doors and the return to dying complicate comfort. Track these changes as part of the soldiers’ mental experience rather than a straightforward trip on leave."
      ],
      [
        "Duty and belief are under pressure",
        "The poem places sacrifice, home, faith and doubt together. Its language can suggest that protection of what is loved no longer makes suffering fully intelligible. The final burial scene and return of the refrain prevent a neat resolution. Avoid reducing the whole poem to either uncomplicated religious confidence or a single definitive statement that belief has vanished."
      ]
    ],
