        "Exposure is organised into eight five-line stanzas. Short final lines often interrupt the longer movement, and a refrain returns at several points rather than closing every stanza in identical words. The repeated shape can make the experience feel cyclical while questions and changes prevent it from being a mechanically fixed pattern."
