        "A third-person account places an unnamed soldier in the middle of running through a field under fire. The opening gives bodily immediacy before a full explanation of context. Do not assume that the awakening must be literal rising from sleep, or that a precise named battle is supplied. Read the whole assigned poem before judging the soldier’s movement."
